  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1200 PM CDT Fri Oct 30 2026\n\nHigh pressure holds dry and warm weather into the first half of\nthe weekend, although high clouds will increase and thicken.\nThat occurs in advance of our first rain chance in awhile. The\nbest chance of rain still looks to be between midnight Saturday\nnight and midday Sunday, when the bulk of the 1/4 to 3/4 inches\nof cumulative rains should fall.\n\nAfter this weekend, daily rain chances carry thru next week,\nwith the best such chances Tuesday into Wednesday. That is when\nthe bulk of the 3/4 to 1.5 inches cumulative rain falls over\nthat time period, with some isolated higher totals upward to 2\ninches possible farther west (Ozarks). \n\nThe onset of these rain chances means temperatures are driven\nback closer to seasonal norms with daily highs next week ranging\nfrom the upper half 60s to lower 70s. Adding to the more\nseasonal autumnal feel will be breezier winds with the\naforementioned parent storm system's approach, arrival, and\ndeparture during the mid week period.",
